---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Reveal from "../components/Reveal.astro";
import "../styles/base.css";
import "../styles/pages/about.css";
---

<Base title={"About · Y2O"} description={"Y2O is a Canadian company building a student-owned record of effort beyond grades, started by a family around one student question."} current="/about">
<header class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 90px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="tag rv">About Y2O</span>
    <h1 class="rv d1">
      Built in Canada, for the work <em>students actually do</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="sub rv d2">
      A Canadian company building a student-owned record of effort beyond
      grades. It started with one student's question and a kitchen table.
    </p>
    <div class="actions rv d3">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="contact.html">Create your account</a
      ><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:info@youth2opportunities.ca"
        >Get in touch</a
      >
    </div>
    <div class="facts rv d3">
      <div class="fact"><b>2026</b><span>Founded</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><b>Live</b><span>Now in Ontario</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><b>50+</b><span>Students building</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><b>Canada</b><span>Data and operations</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="sec soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">What we're building</span>
      <h2 class="h2">One record where every effort counts</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="build">
      <div class="rv">
        <p>
          Grades alone no longer separate strong students. Jobs ask for
          proof of skills, not just paper. And the work happening outside
          school is the work that builds people.
        </p>
        <p>
          Y2O holds all of it. Logged by the student, confirmed by the
          people who saw it, owned by the student for good.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="promise rv d1">
        <small>Our promise</small>
        <div class="m">
          <span>Track it</span><span>Verify it</span
          ><span>Carry it forward</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">The founders</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Built by family. Shaped by students.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Three people, three voices, the same kitchen table.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="team">
      <div class="mem rv">
        <div class="mh">
          <div class="av">V</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Varya</h3>
            <span class="mrole">The student voice</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <q
          >If grades don't show all the work, then where does the work
          go?</q
        >
        <p>
          Asked the question that started Y2O. Keeps the product honest to
          what students will actually use.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mem rv d1">
        <div class="mh">
          <div class="av">V</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Vinay</h3>
            <span class="mrole">The business voice</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <q
          >If a student can prove what they did, the record becomes the
          leverage.</q
        >
        <p>
          Twenty years building businesses and hiring early-career people,
          watching strong candidates lose ground because the paper trail
          didn't keep up.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="mem rv d2">
        <div class="mh">
          <div class="av">P</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Pankaj</h3>
            <span class="mrole">The tech voice</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <q
          >The record has to be simple enough to use, and strong enough to
          trust.</q
        >
        <p>
          Decades designing software that handles trust and verification.
          Makes sure the record is private by default.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">Origin</span>
      <h2 class="h2">The question that started Y2O</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="origin">
      <div class="rv">
        <p>
          Varya was in high school doing what most students do. Saturday
          tutoring, a weekend job, the robotics build team, helping with the
          family business. Stretched thin, doing real work.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of it was on her transcript or a résumé, and she had no way
          to show it on applications.
        </p>
        <p>
          The honest answer to her question was nowhere. So we started
          building somewhere.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="oq rv d1">
        <small>The question</small>
        <p>
          If grades don't show all the work, then where does the work go?
        </p>
        <span>Y2O is the record we wished she'd had in Grade 9.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">What we believe</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Five values every decision has to pass</h2>
      <p class="lead">If a choice doesn't pass these, it doesn't ship.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="vals">
      <div class="val rv">
        <span>01</span>
        <h4>Student-owned</h4>
        <p>The record belongs to the student, after graduation too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="val rv d1">
        <span>02</span>
        <h4>Verified by people</h4>
        <p>A real person who saw the work beats any algorithm.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="val rv d2">
        <span>03</span>
        <h4>Built with partners</h4>
        <p>Coaches, employers, and programs shape confirmation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="val rv d3">
        <span>04</span>
        <h4>Built with students</h4>
        <p>If they wouldn't use it on the bus, we redesign it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="val rv d4">
        <span>05</span>
        <h4>Built for what's next</h4>
        <p>The record has to work past Grade 12.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag on-dark">Built in Canada</span>
      <h2 class="h2">A Canadian company, live in Ontario</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Data and operations in Canada. Starting across the GTA.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="four">
      <div class="chg rv">
        <div class="big">100<em>%</em></div>
        <h4>In Canada</h4>
        <p>Data stored and processed in Canada.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d1">
        <div class="big">PIPEDA</div>
        <h4>Federal privacy law</h4>
        <p>Built to follow Canada's privacy law.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d2">
        <div class="big">0</div>
        <h4>Ads</h4>
        <p>Served to students. Ever.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d3">
        <div class="big">50<em>+</em></div>
        <h4>Students</h4>
        <p>Building their records today.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap faq">
    <div class="rv">
      <span class="tag">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">About the company</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size: 18px">
        Still wondering?
        <a
          href="mailto:info@youth2opportunities.ca"
          style="color: var(--maroon); font-weight: 700"
          >info@youth2opportunities.ca</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="qa rv d1">
      <details open>
        <summary>Is Y2O Canadian?<span class="pl">+</span></summary>
        <p>Yes. Y2O Growth Inc. is a Canadian company, live in Ontario.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Who builds Y2O?<span class="pl">+</span></summary>
        <p>
          A family team: Vinay, Varya, and Pankaj, with students testing
          every change.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why high school?<span class="pl">+</span></summary>
        <p>
          It's when effort beyond class starts to matter, and when it's
          easiest to lose track of.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How can I get involved?<span class="pl">+</span></summary>
        <p>
          Students and organizations can create an account. Schools,
          universities, and employers can email us.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding: 0 0 40px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta rv">
      <div>
        <span class="tag on-dark">Get involved</span>
        <h2>Help us build this right</h2>
        <p>
          Students, families, partners, schools, universities, employers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="contact.html"
          >Create your account</a
        ><a
          class="btn btn-line-light"
          href="mailto:info@youth2opportunities.ca"
          >Get in touch</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
  <Reveal slot="scripts" />
</Base>
